# Frontend environment
#
# VITE_API_MODE
#   `demo` (default) - the console reads bundled fixtures and shows a permanent
#                      "Demo data" chip. Used for design review before the API
#                      exists. Never mistakes fixture rows for pipeline output.
#   `live`           - the console calls the real API.
#
# VITE_API_BASE
#   In `live` mode, leave this EMPTY to call `/api/...` same-origin. A Pages
#   Function at functions/api/[[path]].ts then proxies to the Worker, forwarding
#   the Cloudflare Access assertion header. Same-origin is the intended path: the
#   Access cookie belongs to this hostname, and Cloudflare only adds the
#   assertion header for requests to the protected host.
#
#   Set it to an absolute origin only for local development against a Worker
#   running on localhost. A direct cross-origin call in production would arrive
#   at the Worker with no assertion and be refused as unauthenticated.
#
# There are deliberately no secrets here: the browser bundle carries zero
# credentials (rule R2). Authentication is entirely Cloudflare Access, riding on
# the Access cookie via `credentials: 'include'`.
VITE_API_MODE=demo
VITE_API_BASE=
